  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "# Set conditions to the states and transitions\n\nThis update adds a lot of method to add conditions to states and transitions. \nThis allows to conditionate the execution of a state or transition action, as well as defining when a transition should or should not be taken.\n\nThese methods are all called `OnCondition` add add up to the existing `OnCondition` method on a final state.\nTheir behavior depends on the method that preceded them:\n\n## On a state\n\nWhen the method `OnCondition` follows a call to `SetFinal`, it defines whether the state is final or not depending on the condition.\nWhen the method `OnCondition` follows a call to `SetAction`, it defines whether the action is triggered when the state is activated.\n\n## On a transition\nWhen the method `OnCondition` follows the constructor of the transition, it defines whether the transition can be taken when transitioning from one state to an other.\nWhen the method `OnCondition` follows a call to `SetAction`, it defines whether the action is triggered when the transition is taken.\n\nMore information is given in the [Transitions](Doc/Transitions.md) and [States](Doc/States.md) documentation pages.\n\n\n# Chain methods when defining states\n\nYou can now chain the `SetDefault` with several `AddTransition` calls, as well as chaining the `SetAction` and `SetFinal` methods.\n\n```csharp\nvar state = new State<int>()\n\t.SetDefault(new MyDefaultTransition())\n\t.AddTransition(new MyTransition())\n\t.AddTransition(new MyOtherTransition())\n\t.SetAction(new MyAction())\n\t.SetFinal();\n```\n\nThis gives a lighter and more understandable syntax when defining states. See the [States](Doc/States.md) documentation page for more information and understand better how it works.\n\n# Other\n- Remove the `OverwriteTransition` method from the `State` class to conform with conditional transitions. Use `AddTransition` instead.\n- Correction of some typos in the documentation.",
